  "components": [],
  "overview": "**NewsKit** is a light-first design system anchored on `rgba(243,249,255,1)` canvas surfaces with `#0b0b0c` primary ink (18.6:1 contrast) and `#0b0b0c` brand accent.\n\nTypography centers cleanly on `DM Sans` (80px display down to 17px body), unified by `8px` base corner radius and stepped `rgba(243,249,255,1)` -> `rgba(240,249,253,1)` surface layering.\n\nMaintained by **News Corp**. Source: published token package (https://github.com/newscorp-ghfb/newskit), repo https://github.com/newscorp-ghfb/newskit. Inventory: **91** colors, **25** typography steps, and **0** documented components (see repository license).",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `rgba(243,249,255,1)` (light) with `#0b0b0c` primary text and `#0b0b0c` secondary labels.\n- Use `#0b0b0c` with `#f7f7f8` text (18.4:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `DM Sans` headings with `DM Sans` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Apply `8px` base geometry across inputs and buttons (8px on outer containers).\n- Separate containers via `rgba(240,249,253,1)` surface shifts and `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of light polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not mix conflicting corner radii that clash with the system's `8px` baseline.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `input` fields and secondary buttons."
}
